// Sperrsignal (Lichtsperrsignal) — the shunting signal, Sh 0 / Sh 1 (Ril 301).
//
// It has no main aspect at all: Sh 0 is "Halt! Fahrverbot" and forbids *every* movement,
// train or shunt, and Sh 1 is "Fahrverbot aufgehoben", which lets a shunting movement past
// on sight at 25 km/h. Hp 1 is never shown here, and a main signal's Hp 1 says nothing to a
// shunting movement either — that is the whole difference between the two kinds of
// movement, and it is why a shunt needs a Rangierstraße rather than a Zugstraße.
//
// The interlocking sets `shunting` when a shunting route is locked at this signal; the
// `lamps` strings are what the model shows and are entirely the mod's own.
(
    // The presentation system decides nothing here — a Sperrsignal is in no aspect
    // catalogue of its own — but a signal type has to name one.
    system: Ks,
    rules: [
        // Sh 1: two white lights diagonally. A shunting route is set over it.
        (
            when: (shunting: Some(true)),
            show: (shunt: Some(Proceed)),
            lamps: ["sh1"],
        ),
        // Sh 0: the resting state. Two red lights side by side.
        (
            when: (),
            show: (shunt: Some(Stop)),
            lamps: ["sh0"],
        ),
    ],
    tags: ["shunting", "sperrsignal"],
)
